**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration provisions the necessary AWS infrastructure to deploy a web application. It includes:

- A VPC with an Internet Gateway for network connectivity.
- Two subnets (public and private) within the VPC.
- Route tables and route configurations to enable internet access for the public subnet.
- An IAM role for the Elastic Beanstalk environment and an IAM role for the RDS instance to ensure proper access management.
- An RDS instance for the database, configured with a security group and associated with the appropriate IAM role.
- An Elastic Beanstalk environment to deploy the web application, which will use the VPC, subnets, and RDS instance.

All resources are created within a single AWS region, and default values are provided for variables to ensure the configuration is deployable without additional input.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "vpc_cidr" {
  description = "CIDR block for the VPC"
  default     = "10.0.0.0/16"
}

variable "public_subnet_cidr" {
  description = "CIDR block for the public subnet"
  default     = "10.0.1.0/24"
}

variable "private_subnet_cidr" {
  description = "CIDR block for the private subnet"
  default     = "10.0.2.0/24"
}

variable "rds_instance_type" {
  description = "Type of RDS instance"
  default     = "db.t3.micro"
}

variable "rds_engine" {
  description = "Engine for the RDS instance"
  default     = "mysql"
}

variable "rds_engine_version" {
  description = "Engine version for the RDS instance"
  default     = "5.7"
}

variable "rds_db_name" {
  description = "Database name for the RDS instance"
  default     = "mydb"
}

variable "rds_username" {
  description = "Username for the RDS instance"
  default     = "admin"
}

variable "rds_password" {
  description = "Password for the RDS instance"
  default     = "securepassword"
}

variable "eb_environment_name" {
  description = "Name of the Elastic Beanstalk environment"
  default     = "my-web-app-env"
}

variable "eb_application_name" {
  description = "Name of the Elastic Beanstalk application"
  default     = "my-web-app"
}

variable "eb_solution_stack" {
  description = "Solution stack for Elastic Beanstalk"
  default     = "64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.2.0 running Python 3.10"
}

