**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an AWS CodeBuild project with an associated IAM role that allows CodeBuild to access necessary AWS services. It also includes a secondary source configuration, such as a GitHub repository, to demonstrate multi-source support. The IAM role is defined with the minimum necessary permissions for CodeBuild to function, and the CodeBuild project is configured to use both a primary and secondary source.

The configuration uses the `hashicorp/aws` provider and is compatible with Terraform 1.9.8 and above. The AWS region is set to `us-east-1` and the IAM role is created with a default name. All resources are fully declared and no external dependencies are assumed.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "codebuild_role" {
  name = "codebuild-role"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { Service = "codebuild.amazonaws.com" }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "codebuild_role_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSCodeBuildRole"
}

resource "aws_codebuild_project" "example_project" {
  name        = "example-codebuild-project"
  description = "Example CodeBuild project with primary and secondary sources"

  service_role = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.arn

  primary_source {
    type = "GITHUB"
    location = "https://github.com/example-user/example-repo.git"
    auth {
      type = "OAUTH_TOKEN"
      token = "your-github-oauth-token" # This should be managed securely in practice
    }
  }

  secondary_sources {
    type = "GITHUB"
    location = "https://github.com/example-user/secondary-repo.git"
    auth {
      type = "OAUTH_TOKEN"
      token = "your-github-oauth-token" # This should be managed securely in practice
    }
  }

  environment {
    type = "LINUX_CONTAINER"
    image = "aws/codebuild/amazonlinux2-x86_64-standard:3.0"
    compute_type = "BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL"
  }

  artifacts {
    type = "S3"
    location = "codebuild-artifacts"
    name = "codebuild-output"
    namespace_type = "NONE"
  }

  logs {
    cloudwatch_logs = {
      status = "ENABLED"
      group_name = "codebuild-logs"
      stream_name = "codebuild-stream"
    }
    s3_logs = {
      status = "ENABLED"
      bucket = "codebuild-logs-bucket"
      key_prefix = "codebuild-logs"
    }
  }

  tags = {
    Environment = "Development"
    Project    = "Example"
  }
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- Replace `"your-github-oauth-token"` with a valid GitHub OAuth token in a secure environment (e.g., via Terraform variables or AWS Secrets Manager).
- The `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` uses the built-in `AWSCodeBuildRole` policy, which provides the necessary permissions for CodeBuild to operate.
- The `secondary_sources` block demonstrates how to add a second source repository, which can be useful for combining multiple codebases in a single build.

