**Description:**  
This Terraform configuration defines an AWS Kendra data source with a proxy configuration. The data source is set up to use a specified proxy server for accessing external content. The configuration includes a proxy URL and port, and it uses a default IAM role for the Kendra index. The provider is configured for the `us-east-1` region.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_kendra_data_source" "example" {
  name        = "example-data-source"
  index_id    = "index-12345678"
  type        = "S3"
  proxy_configuration {
    proxy_url = "http://proxy.example.com"
    proxy_port = 8080
  }
}
```

**Note:**  
- Replace `"index-12345678"` with the actual Kendra index ID.
- Ensure that the IAM role used by the Kendra index has the necessary permissions to access the S3 bucket and use the proxy configuration.

