**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates a DAX (DynamoDB Accelerator) cluster using AWS. The cluster will consist of a single node (replication factor = 1) with the node type `dax.r4.large`. The configuration includes:

- A DAX cluster resource with the specified node type and replication factor.
- A provider block configured for AWS in the `us-east-1` region.
- Default values for variables to ensure the configuration is deployable without additional input.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "dax_cluster_name" {
  description = "Name of the DAX cluster"
  default     = "my-dax-cluster"
}

variable "dax_node_type" {
  description = "Type of nodes in the DAX cluster"
  default     = "dax.r4.large"
}

variable "dax_replication_factor" {
  description = "Replication factor for the DAX cluster"
  default     = 1
}

resource "aws_dax_cluster" "dax_cluster" {
  name                   = var.dax_cluster_name
  node_type              = var.dax_node_type
  replication_factor     = var.dax_replication_factor
  iam_role_arn           = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/dax-role"
  subnet_ids             = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-87654321"]
  security_group_ids     = ["sg-12345678"]
  tags = {
    Environment = "production"
  }
}
```

**Note:** Replace the `iam_role_arn`, `subnet_ids`, and `security_group_ids` with your actual AWS IAM role ARN, subnet IDs, and security group IDs. This configuration assumes that the IAM role has the necessary permissions to create and manage a DAX cluster.

