This Terraform configuration sets up a custom Time to Live (TTL) attribute for data expiration in Amazon DynamoDB. It creates a DynamoDB table with a TTL attribute, which allows items in the table to expire automatically after a specified period. The TTL is managed using a DynamoDB Time to Live (TTL) attribute, and the configuration includes a default TTL value of 30 days.

The configuration includes:
- A DynamoDB table with a TTL attribute.
- A default TTL value of 30 days.
- A valid AWS provider configuration in the `us-east-1` region.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "table_name" {
  description = "Name of the DynamoDB table"
  default     = "example-ttl-table"
}

variable "ttl_attribute_name" {
  description = "Name of the TTL attribute"
