**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates a basic AWS VPC with two subnets, one in each of two Availability Zones. It then creates an AWS Redshift subnet group that includes these subnets. A basic Redshift cluster is created and associated with the subnet group. The cluster is configured with a public endpoint for access. All resources are created in the `us-east-1` region, and appropriate IAM roles and permissions are defined to ensure the cluster can be created and managed.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "vpc_cidr" {
  description = "CIDR block for the VPC"
  default     = "10.0.0.0/16"
}

variable "subnet_cidr_1" {
  description = "CIDR block for the first subnet"
  default     = "10.0.1.0/24"
}

variable "subnet_cidr_2" {
  description = "CIDR block for the second subnet"
  default     = "10.0.2.0/24"
}

variable "redshift_cluster_identifier" {
  description = "Identifier for the Redshift cluster"
  default     = "example-redshift-cluster"
}

variable "redshift_master_username" {
  description = "Master username for the Redshift cluster"
  default     = "admin"
}

variable "redshift_master_password" {
  description = "Master password for the Redshift cluster"
  default     = "SecureP@ssw0rd!"
}

variable "redshift_cluster_type" {
  description = "Type of Redshift cluster (e.g., 'single-node')"
  default     = "single-node"
}

variable "redshift_node_type" {
  description = "Node type for the Redshift cluster (e.g., 'dc2.large')"
  default     = "dc2.large"
}

