**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates two basic AWS IAM users and assigns them to a single IAM group. The IAM group is created with basic permissions, and the IAM users are created with default passwords. The configuration uses the `aws_iam_group`, `aws_iam_user`, and `aws_iam_user_group_membership` resources to achieve this. The AWS provider is configured with a default region, and all necessary IAM roles and permissions are defined within the configuration.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "group_name" {
  description = "Name of the IAM group"
  default     = "BasicUsersGroup"
}

variable "user_names" {
  description = "List of IAM user names to create"
  default     = ["user1", "user2"]
}

variable "user_passwords" {
  description = "List of passwords for the IAM users"
  default     = ["Password123!", "Password123!"]
  sensitive  = true
}

resource "aws_iam_group" "basic_group" {
  name = var.group_name
}

resource "aws_iam_user" "basic_users" {
  count = length(var.user_names)
  name  = var.user_names[count.index]

  password = var.user_passwords[count.index]
  password_reset_required = true
}

resource "aws_iam_user_group_membership" "user_group_membership" {
  count         = length(var.user_names)
  user         = var.user_names[count.index]
  group        = aws_iam_group.basic_group.name
  permissions   = ["iam:ListGroups", "iam:ListUsers"]
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- The `aws_iam_group` resource creates a group with a default name.
- The `aws_iam_user` resource creates two users with default passwords.
- The `aws_iam_user_group_membership` resource adds each user to the group and grants basic permissions.
- All variables have default values for easy deployment.
- The AWS provider is configured with the `us-west-2` region. You can change this as needed.

