**Description:**

This Terraform configuration creates an Amazon S3 bucket with the setting that the **bucket owner pays for fees**. This is achieved by setting the `bucket_ownership_controls` block with `owner_id` set to the AWS account ID of the bucket owner. The configuration includes a valid AWS provider block with a specified region, and the S3 bucket is created in that region.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "bucket_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 bucket."
  default     = "my-terraform-bucket"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "example_bucket" {
  bucket = var.bucket_name

  # Ensure the bucket owner pays for fees
  ownership_controls {
    owner_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id
    rules {
      object_ownership = "BucketOwnerPreferred"
      bucket_owner     = "BucketOwner"
    }
  }

