**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration sets up the necessary AWS infrastructure to support an autograder for a CS class using AWS CodeBuild. The infrastructure includes:

- A CodeBuild project that runs the autograder code.
- An IAM role for CodeBuild to access required AWS services (e.g., S3, EC2, etc.).
- A CodePipeline (optional) to trigger the CodeBuild project from GitHub.
- An S3 bucket to store student submissions and autograder results.
- A CodeBuild role with appropriate permissions to access the S3 bucket and run the build process.

The configuration uses AWS CodeBuild to run the autograder, which pulls code from a GitHub repository, executes tests, and stores the results in an S3 bucket. The CodeBuild project is configured to run in a specific AWS region, and all necessary IAM roles and policies are defined to ensure secure and functional execution.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "github_repository" {
  description = "The GitHub repository URL for the autograder code."
  default     = "https://github.com/example/autograder.git"
}

variable "s3_bucket_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 bucket to store student submissions and results."
  default     = "autograder-results-bucket"
}

variable "codebuild_role_name" {
  description = "The name of the IAM role for CodeBuild."
  default     = "CodeBuildAutograderRole"
}

variable "codebuild_project_name" {
  description = "The name of the CodeBuild project."
  default     = "AutograderCodeBuildProject"
}

variable "codebuild_timeout_in_minutes" {
  description = "The timeout for the CodeBuild project in minutes."
  default     = 10
}

variable "codebuild_service_role_arn" {
  description = "The ARN of the IAM role for CodeBuild."
  default     = ""
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "codebuild_role" {
  name = var.codebuild_role_name

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = {
        Service = "codebuild.amazonaws.com"
      }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "codebuild_role_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSCodeBuildRole"
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "codebuild_s3_access" {
  name = "${var.codebuild_role_name}-s3-access"

  role = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.name

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Action = [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:ListBucket"
      ]
      Resource = [
        "arn:aws:s3:::${var.s3_bucket_name}",
        "arn:aws:s3:::${var.s3_bucket_name}/*"
      ]
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "results_bucket" {
  bucket = var.s3_bucket_name
  acl    = "private"
}

resource "aws_codebuild_project" "autograder_project" {
  name    = var.codebuild_project_name
  service_role = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.arn

  environment {
    type = "LINUX_CONTAINER"
    image = "aws/codebuild/amazonlinux2-x86_64-standard:3.0"
    compute_type = "BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL"
  }

  source {
    type = "GITHUB"
    location = var.github_repository
    git_submodules = false
  }

  artifacts {
    type = "S3"
    location = var.s3_bucket_name
    name = "autograder-results"
  }

  timeout_in_minutes = var.codebuild_timeout_in_minutes

  logs {
    cloudwatch = true
  }
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- This configuration assumes that the GitHub repository is public or that the CodeBuild project has the necessary permissions to access it.
- The `codebuild_service_role_arn` variable is optional and can be used if you want to use an existing IAM role for CodeBuild.
- The CodeBuild project is configured to run in the `us-east-1` region, but this can be changed by modifying the `region` parameter in the `provider` block.
- The S3 bucket is created with private access, and the CodeBuild role has read/write access to it.
- The CodeBuild project uses a standard Amazon Linux 2 image and runs in a small compute environment, which is suitable for most autograding tasks.

