**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration sets up the infrastructure for a video streaming site that distributes video content globally using AWS services. The solution includes:

- **AWS S3**: To store the video content in a secure, scalable, and durable storage bucket.
- **AWS CloudFront**: To deliver video content with low latency and high transfer speed to users around the world.
- **AWS Route53**: To manage the domain name and route traffic to the CloudFront distribution.
- **AWS IAM**: To create necessary roles and policies for secure access to the services.
- **AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)**: To provision an SSL certificate for secure HTTPS connections.

The configuration includes:
- A private S3 bucket for video storage.
- A CloudFront distribution with the S3 bucket as the origin.
- A Route53 hosted zone and record to point the domain to the CloudFront distribution.
- An ACM certificate for the domain.
- IAM roles and policies to allow CloudFront to access the S3 bucket.

All resources are configured in the `us-east-1` region, and default values are provided for variables to make the configuration deployable out of the box.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "domain_name" {
  description = "The domain name for the video streaming site."
  default     = "example.com"
}

variable "s3_bucket_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 bucket to store video content."
  default     = "video-streaming-bucket"
}

variable "cloudfront_distribution_name" {
  description = "The name of the CloudFront distribution."
  default     = "video-streaming-distribution"
}

variable "certificate_arn" {
  description = "The ARN of the ACM certificate for the domain."
  default     = "arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:123456789012:certificate/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"
}

variable "route53_zone_id" {
  description = "The Route53 hosted zone ID for the domain."
  default     = "Z123456789012345678"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_bucket" {
  bucket = var.s3_bucket_name
  acl    = "private"

  lifecycle {
    prevent_destroy = true
  }

  tags = {
    Name        = "video-streaming-bucket"
    Environment = "production"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "video_bucket_policy" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/CloudFrontOriginAccessIdentity" }
        Action = [
          "s3:GetObject",
        ]
        Resource = "${aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.arn}/*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

