**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration sets up a Lightsail storage unit and links it with a Lightsail compute service. The configuration includes:

- A Lightsail compute instance (server) with a default name and basic configuration.
- A Lightsail storage unit (block storage) with a default name and size.
- A Lightsail attachment that links the storage unit to the compute instance.
- All resources are created in the `us-east-1` region.
- Default values are provided for variables such as instance name, storage size, and region.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "instance_name" {
  description = "Name of the Lightsail compute instance"
  default     = "lightsail-instance"
}

variable "storage_name" {
  description = "Name of the Lightsail storage unit"
  default     = "lightsail-storage"
}

variable "storage_size" {
  description = "Size of the Lightsail storage unit in GB"
  default     = 20
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "lightsail_instance" {
  name              = var.instance_name
  availability_zone = "us-east-1a"
  blueprint_id      = "ubuntu_22_04"
  bundle_id         = "micro_1_0"
  key_pair_name     = "default"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_storage_bucket" "lightsail_storage" {
  name     = var.storage_name
  size_in_gb = var.storage_size
}

resource "aws_lightsail_attachment" "lightsail_attachment" {
  instance_name = aws_lightsail_instance.lightsail_instance.name
  storage_name  = aws_lightsail_storage_bucket.lightsail_storage.name
}
```

---

**Note:** This configuration assumes that the default key pair (`default`) is already available in your AWS account. If not, you may need to create or import a key pair separately.

