**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an AWS S3 bucket designed for long-term data storage and backup. The bucket is configured with versioning, server-side encryption, and lifecycle policies to ensure data durability, security, and cost efficiency. It also includes an IAM role to manage access to the bucket, ensuring secure and controlled access.

The configuration includes:
- An AWS S3 bucket with versioning and encryption enabled.
- A lifecycle policy to transition objects to Glacier for long-term storage.
- An IAM role with permissions to manage the bucket and its contents.
- A default region (us-east-1) and default bucket name (`long-term-backup-bucket`).

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "bucket_name" {
  description = "Name of the S3 bucket for long-term storage and backup"
  default     = "long-term-backup-bucket"
}

variable "environment" {
  description = "Environment name (e.g., dev, prod)"
  default     = "prod"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "long_term_backup" {
  bucket = var.bucket_name
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }

  server_side_encryption_configuration {
    rule {
      apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {
        sse_algorithm = "AES256"
      }
    }
  }

  lifecycle_rule {
    id      = "TransitionToGlacier"
    enabled = true

    prefix = ""

    transition {
      days = 30
      storage_class = "GLACIER"
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "s3_access_role" {
  name = "s3-access-role-${var.environment}"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = {
        Service = "s3.amazonaws.com"
      }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "s3_access_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.s3_access_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3FullAccess"
}
```

---

This configuration is ready to be deployed using Terraform 1.9.8 or later and the `hashicorp/aws` provider version 5.75 or later. It ensures secure, encrypted, and cost-effective long-term storage and backup of data in AWS S3.

