**Description:**

This Terraform configuration creates a Gateway Load Balancer (GLB) in AWS. A Gateway Load Balancer is used to route traffic to an Application Load Balancer (ALB) or Network Load Balancer (NLB) based on the destination port. This configuration includes the necessary AWS provider setup, a VPC, and the Gateway Load Balancer resource. The configuration is designed to be deployable in AWS using Terraform version 1.9.8 or higher and the hashicorp/aws provider version 5.75 or higher.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "vpc_id" {
  description = "The ID of the VPC to associate with the Gateway Load Balancer."
  default     = "vpc-12345678"
}

variable "gateway_load_balancer_name" {
  description = "The name of the Gateway Load Balancer."
  default     = "glb-example"
}

resource "aws_gateway_load_balancer" "example" {
  name                = var.gateway_load_balancer_name
  vpc_id              = var.vpc_id
  subnet_ids          = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-87654321"]
  ip_address_type     = "ipv4"
  tags = {
    Environment = "production"
    Project     = "example"
  }
}
```

