**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration creates an AWS Elastic File System (EFS) with automatic backups enabled. It includes the necessary AWS provider configuration, sets up the EFS file system, and enables automatic backups with a specified retention period. The configuration also defines a default retention period for backups and ensures the EFS is created in a specified AWS region.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "efs_name" {
  description = "Name of the EFS file system"
  default     = "my-efs"
}

variable "backup_retention_days" {
  description = "Number of days to retain backups"
  default     = 7
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system" "efs" {
  creation_token = var.efs_name
  name           = var.efs_name
  lifecycle_policy {
    transition_to_ia_days = 30
  }
  tags = {
    Environment = "production"
  }
}

resource "aws_efs_backup_policy" "efs_backup" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.efs.id
  backup_policy {
    backup_window_start_time {
      hours   = 18
      minutes = 0
    }
    retention_days = var.backup_retention_days
  }
}
```

---

This configuration is deployable with Terraform version 1.9.8 or higher and uses the `hashicorp/aws` provider version 5.75 or higher. It creates an EFS with automatic backups enabled and includes default values for variables to ensure it is self-contained and ready to deploy.

